# Caching Strategies Guidelines

## Mục tiêu

Tài liệu này định nghĩa các nguyên tắc và best practices cho việc implement caching strategies trong Cursor Enterprise Framework. Mục tiêu là tối ưu hóa application performance, reduce database load, và improve response times thông qua việc sử dụng caching hiệu quả.

Caching là kỹ thuật lưu trữ copies của data hoặc computation results để future requests có thể được served nhanh hơn. Việc implement caching đúng cách có thể improve performance đáng kể trong khi vẫn đảm bảo data consistency.

## Nguyên tắc cơ bản

### 1. Cache Hierarchy

Understand different cache levels.

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                    Cache Hierarchy                          │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│                                                             │
│  Level 1: Application Cache (In-Memory)                    │
│  ├── Fastest access (< 1ms)                                │
│  ├── Limited size (MB)                                     │
│  └── Process-specific                                      │
│                                                             │
│  Level 2: Distributed Cache (Redis/Memcached)              │
│  ├── Fast access (1-10ms)                                  │
│  ├── Larger size (GB)                                      │
│  └── Shared across instances                               │
│                                                             │
│  Level 3: Database Cache                                   │
│  ├── Query cache                                           │
│  ├── Buffer pool                                           │
│  └── Connection pool                                       │
│                                                             │
│  Level 4: CDN Cache                                        │
│  ├── Static assets                                         │
│  ├── Edge locations                                        │
│  └── Geographic distribution                               │
│                                                             │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### 2. Cache Patterns

Common caching patterns và use cases.

```typescript
// Cache-Aside Pattern (Lazy Loading)
class CacheAsideService<T> {
    constructor(
        private cache: CacheClient,
        private db: Database,
        private ttl: number = 3600
    ) {}

    async get(key: string, fetcher: () => Promise<T>): Promise<T> {
        // Try cache first
        const cached = await this.cache.get(key);
        if (cached) {
            return JSON.parse(cached);
        }

        // Cache miss - fetch from source
        const data = await fetcher();

        // Store in cache
        await this.cache.setex(key, this.ttl, JSON.stringify(data));

        return data;
    }

    async invalidate(key: string): Promise<void> {
        await this.cache.del(key);
    }

    async refresh(key: string, fetcher: () => Promise<T>): Promise<T> {
        // Invalidate first
        await this.invalidate(key);

        // Fetch fresh data
        const data = await fetcher();

        // Store in cache
        await this.cache.setex(key, this.ttl, JSON.stringify(data));

        return data;
    }
}

// Read-Through Pattern
class ReadThroughCache {
    async get(key: string): Promise<any> {
        const cached = await this.cache.get(key);
        if (cached) {
            return cached;
        }

        const data = await this.db.read(key);
        await this.cache.set(key, data);
        return data;
    }
}

// Write-Through Pattern
class WriteThroughCache {
    async set(key: string, data: any): Promise<void> {
        await this.db.write(key, data);
        await this.cache.set(key, data);
    }

    async delete(key: string): Promise<void> {
        await this.db.delete(key);
        await this.cache.del(key);
    }
}

// Write-Behind Pattern
class WriteBehindCache {
    private queue: Queue;

    async set(key: string, data: any): Promise<void> {
        await this.cache.set(key, data);
        await this.queue.enqueue('db-write', { key, data });
    }
}
```

### 3. Cache Key Design

Design cache keys for optimal performance.

```typescript
// Cache key conventions
class CacheKeyBuilder {
    static readonly SEPARATOR = ':';

    static resource(resource: string, id: string): string {
        return `${resource}${this.SEPARATOR}${id}`;
    }

    static resourceList(resource: string, params?: Record<string, any>): string {
        const sortedParams = params ? Object.keys(params).sort().map(
            k => `${k}=${params[k]}`
        ).join('&') : '';
        return `${resource}${this.SEPARATOR}list${sortedParams ? this.SEPARATOR + sortedParams : ''}`;
    }

    static userResource(userId: string, resource: string, id: string): string {
        return `user${this.SEPARATOR}${userId}${this.SEPARATOR}${resource}${this.SEPARATOR}${id}`;
    }

    static versioned(key: string, version: number): string {
        return `${key}${this.SEPARATOR}v${version}`;
    }

    static pagination(
        resource: string,
        params: { page?: number; limit?: number; sort?: string }
    ): string {
        return `${resource}${this.SEPARATOR}p${params.page || 1}${this.SEPARATOR}l${params.limit || 20}`;
    }
}

// Usage
const userKey = CacheKeyBuilder.resource('user', '123');                    // user:123
const userListKey = CacheKeyBuilder.resourceList('users', { role: 'admin' }); // users:list&role=admin
const userPostKey = CacheKeyBuilder.userResource('123', 'post', '456');       // user:123:post:456
```

### 4. TTL Configuration

Configure TTL based on data characteristics.

```typescript
// TTL configuration by data type
const TTL_CONFIG = {
    // Static reference data - long TTL
    'country': 86400 * 30,           // 30 days
    'language': 86400 * 30,          // 30 days
    'category': 86400 * 7,          // 7 days

    // User-specific data - medium TTL
    'user:profile': 3600,           // 1 hour
    'user:settings': 3600 * 6,      // 6 hours
    'user:permissions': 3600,       // 1 hour

    // Session data - short TTL
    'session': 1800,                // 30 minutes
    'token': 900,                  // 15 minutes
    'rate_limit': 60,              // 1 minute

    // Content - variable TTL
    'post': 3600,                  // 1 hour
    'post:popular': 300,           // 5 minutes
    'comment': 1800,               // 30 minutes

    // Metrics - very short TTL
    'metrics:daily': 3600,         // 1 hour
    'metrics:realtime': 60,       // 1 minute
    'leaderboard': 300,           // 5 minutes
};

// TTL Strategy
class TTLStrategy {
    static forResource(type: string): number {
        return TTL_CONFIG[type] || 3600;
    }

    static withJitter(ttl: number): number {
        // Add random jitter (±10%) to prevent cache stampede
        const jitter = ttl * 0.1;
        return ttl + Math.floor((Math.random() * 2 - 1) * jitter);
    }

    static adaptive(
        accessCount: number,
        lastAccess: Date,
        baseTTL: number
    ): number {
        // Frequently accessed data gets longer TTL
        if (accessCount > 1000) {
            return baseTTL * 2;
        }
        if (accessCount > 100) {
            return baseTTL * 1.5;
        }
        return baseTTL;
    }
}
```

### 5. Cache Invalidation

Implement proper cache invalidation strategies.

```typescript
// Direct invalidation
class CacheInvalidator {
    constructor(private cache: CacheClient) {}

    async invalidate(key: string): Promise<void> {
        await this.cache.del(key);
    }

    async invalidatePattern(pattern: string): Promise<void> {
        const keys = await this.cache.keys(pattern);
        if (keys.length > 0) {
            await this.cache.del(...keys);
        }
    }

    async invalidateByPrefix(prefix: string): Promise<void> {
        await this.invalidatePattern(`${prefix}*`);
    }
}

// Event-driven invalidation
class EventDrivenCacheInvalidator {
    constructor(
        private cache: CacheClient,
        private eventBus: EventBus
    ) {
        this.subscribeToEvents();
    }

    private subscribeToEvents(): void {
        this.eventBus.subscribe('user.updated', async (event) => {
            const { userId } = event.data;
            await Promise.all([
                this.cache.del(`user:${userId}`),
                this.cache.del(`user:${userId}:profile`),
                this.cache.invalidateByPrefix(`users:list*`)
            ]);
        });

        this.eventBus.subscribe('post.created', async (event) => {
            const { post } = event.data;
            await Promise.all([
                this.cache.invalidateByPrefix(`post:${post.id}`),
                this.cache.invalidateByPrefix(`user:${post.authorId}:posts`),
                this.cache.invalidateByPrefix(`posts:list*`)
            ]);
        });
    }
}

// Time-based expiration with refresh
class CacheWithRefresh {
    constructor(
        private cache: CacheClient,
        private ttl: number
    ) {}

    async getOrRefresh(
        key: string,
        fetcher: () => Promise<any>
    ): Promise<any> {
        const cached = await this.cache.get(key);
        const metadata = await this.cache.hgetall(`${key}:meta`);

        if (cached) {
            // Check if refresh needed (stale-while-revalidate)
            if (this.shouldRefresh(metadata)) {
                // Return cached data, refresh in background
                this.refreshInBackground(key, fetcher);
            }
            return JSON.parse(cached);
        }

        // No cache - fetch and cache
        const data = await fetcher();
        await this.cache.setex(key, this.ttl, JSON.stringify(data));
        await this.cache.hset(`${key}:meta`, {
            cachedAt: Date.now().toString(),
            accessCount: '0'
        });

        return data;
    }

    private shouldRefresh(metadata: Record<string, string>): boolean {
        if (!metadata.cachedAt) return true;

        const age = Date.now() - parseInt(metadata.cachedAt);
        const refreshThreshold = this.ttl * 0.8; // Refresh at 80% of TTL

        return age > refreshThreshold;
    }

    private async refreshInBackground(key: string, fetcher: () => Promise<any>): Promise<void> {
        try {
            const data = await fetcher();
            await this.cache.setex(key, this.ttl, JSON.stringify(data));
        } catch (error) {
            console.error('Background refresh failed:', error);
        }
    }
}
```

### 6. Distributed Caching

Redis-based distributed cache implementation.

```typescript
// Redis cache client
class RedisCacheClient implements CacheClient {
    constructor(private redis: Redis) {}

    async get<T>(key: string): Promise<T | null> {
        const value = await this.redis.get(key);
        return value ? JSON.parse(value) : null;
    }

    async set(key: string, value: any, ttl?: number): Promise<void> {
        const serialized = JSON.stringify(value);
        if (ttl) {
            await this.redis.setex(key, ttl, serialized);
        } else {
            await this.redis.set(key, serialized);
        }
    }

    async del(key: string): Promise<void> {
        await this.redis.del(key);
    }

    async mget<T>(keys: string[]): Promise<(T | null)[]> {
        const values = await this.redis.mget(...keys);
        return values.map(v => v ? JSON.parse(v) : null);
    }

    async mset(entries: Record<string, any>, ttl?: number): Promise<void> {
        const pipeline = this.redis.pipeline();

        for (const [key, value] of Object.entries(entries)) {
            const serialized = JSON.stringify(value);
            if (ttl) {
                pipeline.setex(key, ttl, serialized);
            } else {
                pipeline.set(key, serialized);
            }
        }

        await pipeline.exec();
    }

    async keys(pattern: string): Promise<string[]> {
        return this.redis.keys(pattern);
    }
}

// Distributed locking
class DistributedLock {
    constructor(private redis: Redis) {}

    async acquire(
        key: string,
        ttl: number = 10000
    ): Promise<string | null> {
        const lockKey = `lock:${key}`;
        const lockValue = nanoid();

        const acquired = await this.redis.set(
            lockKey,
            lockValue,
            'PX',
            ttl,
            'NX'
        );

        return acquired ? lockValue : null;
    }

    async release(key: string, value: string): Promise<boolean> {
        const lockKey = `lock:${key}`;

        // Use Lua script for atomic check-and-delete
        const script = `
            if redis.call("get", KEYS[1]) == ARGV[1] then
                return redis.call("del", KEYS[1])
            else
                return 0
            end
        `;

        const result = await this.redis.eval(script, 1, lockKey, value);
        return result === 1;
    }

    async withLock<T>(
        key: string,
        fn: () => Promise<T>,
        ttl: number = 10000
    ): Promise<T> {
        const lockValue = await this.acquire(key, ttl);

        if (!lockValue) {
            throw new Error(`Failed to acquire lock for ${key}`);
        }

        try {
            return await fn();
        } finally {
            await this.release(key, lockValue);
        }
    }
}

// Cache stampede prevention
class CacheStampedeProtection {
    constructor(
        private cache: CacheClient,
        private lock: DistributedLock
    ) {}

    async getOrCompute<T>(
        key: string,
        compute: () => Promise<T>,
        ttl: number
    ): Promise<T> {
        const cached = await this.cache.get<T>(key);
        if (cached !== null) {
            return cached;
        }

        // Try to acquire lock
        const lockValue = await this.lock.acquire(`stampede:${key}`, 5000);

        if (!lockValue) {
            // Another process is computing, wait and retry
            await this.sleep(100);
            return this.getOrCompute(key, compute, ttl);
        }

        try {
            // Double-check after acquiring lock
            const cached = await this.cache.get<T>(key);
            if (cached !== null) {
                return cached;
            }

            // Compute and cache
            const value = await compute();
            await this.cache.set(key, value, ttl);
            return value;
        } finally {
            await this.lock.release(`stampede:${key}`, lockValue);
        }
    }

    private sleep(ms: number): Promise<void> {
        return new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, ms));
    }
}
```

### 7. Multi-Layer Caching

Implement multi-layer caching strategy.

```typescript
// Multi-layer cache
class MultiLayerCache {
    constructor(
        private l1: MemoryCache,  // In-memory
        private l2: RedisCache,   // Redis
        private l3: Database     // Database
    ) {}

    async get<T>(key: string): Promise<T | null> {
        // Check L1 first
        let value = await this.l1.get<T>(key);
        if (value !== null) {
            return value;
        }

        // Check L2
        value = await this.l2.get<T>(key);
        if (value !== null) {
            // Populate L1 from L2
            await this.l1.set(key, value, 60); // Short TTL for L1
            return value;
        }

        return null;
    }

    async set<T>(key: string, value: T, l1Ttl: number, l2Ttl: number): Promise<void> {
        // Set in both layers
        await Promise.all([
            this.l1.set(key, value, l1Ttl),
            this.l2.set(key, value, l2Ttl)
        ]);
    }

    async invalidate(key: string): Promise<void> {
        await Promise.all([
            this.l1.invalidate(key),
            this.l2.invalidate(key)
        ]);
    }
}

// Memory cache with LRU
class MemoryCache {
    private cache: Map<string, CacheEntry>;
    private maxSize: number;

    constructor(maxSize: number = 1000) {
        this.cache = new Map();
        this.maxSize = maxSize;
    }

    async get<T>(key: string): Promise<T | null> {
        const entry = this.cache.get(key);

        if (!entry) {
            return null;
        }

        if (entry.expiresAt < Date.now()) {
            this.cache.delete(key);
            return null;
        }

        // Move to end (most recently used)
        this.cache.delete(key);
        this.cache.set(key, entry);

        return entry.value as T;
    }

    async set<T>(key: string, value: T, ttl: number): Promise<void> {
        // Evict if at max size
        if (this.cache.size >= this.maxSize && !this.cache.has(key)) {
            const firstKey = this.cache.keys().next().value;
            this.cache.delete(firstKey);
        }

        this.cache.set(key, {
            value,
            expiresAt: Date.now() + ttl * 1000
        });
    }

    async invalidate(key: string): Promise<void> {
        this.cache.delete(key);
    }
}
```

### 8. Query Caching

Cache database query results.

```typescript
// Query cache
class QueryCache {
    constructor(
        private cache: CacheClient,
        private defaultTTL: number = 300
    ) {}

    async getQuery<T>(
        query: string,
        params: any[],
        fetcher: () => Promise<T>
    ): Promise<T> {
        const cacheKey = this.buildCacheKey(query, params);

        const cached = await this.cache.get<T>(cacheKey);
        if (cached !== null) {
            return cached;
        }

        const result = await fetcher();
        await this.cache.set(cacheKey, result, this.defaultTTL);

        return result;
    }

    private buildCacheKey(query: string, params: any[]): string {
        const normalizedQuery = query.replace(/\s+/g, ' ').trim();
        const paramsHash = crypto.createHash('md5')
            .update(JSON.stringify(params))
            .digest('hex');
        return `query:${crypto.createHash('md5')
            .update(normalizedQuery)
            .digest('hex')}:${paramsHash}`;
    }

    async invalidateByTable(tableName: string): Promise<void> {
        await this.cache.invalidateByPrefix(`query:*:${tableName}*`);
    }

    async invalidateByPattern(pattern: string): Promise<void> {
        await this.cache.invalidateByPrefix(`query:${pattern}`);
    }
}

// ORM integration
class CachedModel<T> {
    constructor(
        private model: Model<T>,
        private queryCache: QueryCache
    ) {}

    async findAll(options?: FindOptions): Promise<T[]> {
        return this.queryCache.getQuery(
            'findAll',
            [options],
            () => this.model.findAll(options)
        );
    }

    async findById(id: string): Promise<T | null> {
        return this.queryCache.getQuery(
            `findById:${id}`,
            [],
            () => this.model.findById(id)
        );
    }

    async create(data: Partial<T>): Promise<T> {
        const result = await this.model.create(data);
        await this.queryCache.invalidateByTable(this.model.tableName);
        return result;
    }
}
```

### 9. Cache Monitoring

Monitor cache health và performance.

```typescript
// Cache metrics
interface CacheMetrics {
    hits: number;
    misses: number;
    hitRate: number;
    evictions: number;
    memoryUsage: number;
    keyCount: number;
}

class CacheMonitor {
    constructor(
        private cache: CacheClient,
        private metrics: MetricsCollector
    ) {
        this.startCollection();
    }

    private startCollection(): void {
        setInterval(async () => {
            await this.collectMetrics();
        }, 60000); // Every minute
    }

    async collectMetrics(): Promise<CacheMetrics> {
        const info = await this.cache.getInfo();

        const hits = parseInt(info.keyspace_hits || '0');
        const misses = parseInt(info.keyspace_misses || '0');
        const total = hits + misses;

        const metrics: CacheMetrics = {
            hits,
            misses,
            hitRate: total > 0 ? (hits / total) * 100 : 0,
            evictions: parseInt(info.evicted_keys || '0'),
            memoryUsage: parseInt(info.used_memory || '0'),
            keyCount: parseInt(info.db0?.keys || '0')
        };

        // Send to metrics collector
        await this.metrics.gauge('cache.hit_rate', metrics.hitRate);
        await this.metrics.gauge('cache.memory_usage', metrics.memoryUsage);
        await this.metrics.gauge('cache.key_count', metrics.keyCount);

        return metrics;
    }

    async getCacheStats(): Promise<CacheStats> {
        const metrics = await this.collectMetrics();

        return {
            hitRate: `${metrics.hitRate.toFixed(2)}%`,
            totalKeys: metrics.keyCount,
            memoryUsed: this.formatBytes(metrics.memoryUsage),
            evictions: metrics.evictions
        };
    }

    private formatBytes(bytes: number): string {
        if (bytes < 1024) return `${bytes}B`;
        if (bytes < 1024 * 1024) return `${(bytes / 1024).toFixed(2)}KB`;
        if (bytes < 1024 * 1024 * 1024) return `${(bytes / (1024 * 1024)).toFixed(2)}MB`;
        return `${(bytes / (1024 * 1024 * 1024)).toFixed(2)}GB`;
    }
}

// Health check
class CacheHealthCheck {
    async check(): Promise<HealthStatus> {
        try {
            await this.cache.ping();
            return { healthy: true, latency: await this.measureLatency() };
        } catch (error) {
            return { healthy: false, error: error.message };
        }
    }

    private async measureLatency(): Promise<number> {
        const start = Date.now();
        await this.cache.ping();
        return Date.now() - start;
    }
}
```

### 10. Session Caching

Implement session storage with caching.

```typescript
// Session cache
interface Session {
    id: string;
    userId: string;
    data: Record<string, any>;
    createdAt: Date;
    expiresAt: Date;
}

class SessionCache {
    constructor(
        private cache: CacheClient,
        private ttl: number = 1800 // 30 minutes
    ) {}

    async create(userId: string, data: Record<string, any> = {}): Promise<Session> {
        const session: Session = {
            id: nanoid(32),
            userId,
            data,
            createdAt: new Date(),
            expiresAt: new Date(Date.now() + this.ttl * 1000)
        };

        await this.cache.setex(
            `session:${session.id}`,
            this.ttl,
            JSON.stringify(session)
        );

        // Add to user's session set
        await this.cache.sadd(`user:${userId}:sessions`, session.id);
        await this.cache.expire(`user:${userId}:sessions`, this.ttl);

        return session;
    }

    async get(sessionId: string): Promise<Session | null> {
        const data = await this.cache.get(`session:${sessionId}`);
        return data ? JSON.parse(data) : null;
    }

    async update(sessionId: string, data: Partial<Session>): Promise<Session | null> {
        const session = await this.get(sessionId);
        if (!session) return null;

        const updated = { ...session, ...data };
        await this.cache.setex(
            `session:${sessionId}`,
            this.ttl,
            JSON.stringify(updated)
        );

        return updated;
    }

    async delete(sessionId: string): Promise<void> {
        const session = await this.get(sessionId);
        if (session) {
            await this.cache.srem(`user:${session.userId}:sessions`, sessionId);
        }
        await this.cache.del(`session:${sessionId}`);
    }

    async deleteAllUserSessions(userId: string): Promise<void> {
        const sessionIds = await this.cache.smembers(`user:${userId}:sessions`);
        for (const id of sessionIds) {
            await this.cache.del(`session:${id}`);
        }
        await this.cache.del(`user:${userId}:sessions`);
    }

    async refresh(sessionId: string): Promise<Session | null> {
        const session = await this.get(sessionId);
        if (!session) return null;

        session.expiresAt = new Date(Date.now() + this.ttl * 1000);
        await this.cache.setex(
            `session:${sessionId}`,
            this.ttl,
            JSON.stringify(session)
        );

        return session;
    }
}
```

